roduces what the video shows."}, {"lit": "person", "meaning": "duine: person (lenited after de: dhuine)", "ctx": "The video is of a person singing."}, {"lit": "at", "meaning": "ag: at", "ctx": "Marks the verbal noun canadh, singing."}, {"lit": "singing", "meaning": "can: to sing (verbal noun: canadh)", "ctx": "Describes the person singing."}, {"lit": "the", "meaning": "an: the", "ctx": "Marks amhráin as definite."}, {"lit": "of the song", "meaning": "amhrán: song (genitive: amhráin)", "ctx": "The person is singing the song."}, {"lit": "will get", "meaning": "faigh: to get (future: gheobhaidh)", "ctx": "Says what the winner will receive."}, {"lit": "the", "meaning": "an: the", "ctx": "Marks buaiteoir as definite."}, {"lit": "winner", "meaning": "buaiteoir: winner", "ctx": "The person who receives the prize."}, {"lit": "prize", "meaning": "duais: prize", "ctx": "What the winner gets."}, {"lit": "1,000", "meaning": "míle: thousand", "ctx": "Gives the prize amount."}, {"lit": "euro", "meaning": "euro: euro", "ctx": "The currency of the prize."}, {"lit": "is", "meaning": "bí: to be (present: tá)", "ctx": "Starts the sentence about information being available."}, {"lit": "all", "meaning": "gach: every, all", "ctx": "Qualifies the information as all information."}, {"lit": "information", "meaning": "eolas: information", "ctx": "The thing that is available."}, {"lit": "under the", "meaning": "faoi + an: under the, about the (faoin)", "ctx": "Means about the competition."}, {"lit": "competition", "meaning": "comórtas: competition (eclipsed: gcomórtas)", "ctx": "The information is about the competition."}, {"lit": "on", "meaning": "ar: on", "ctx": "Part of ar fáil, available."}, {"lit": "available", "meaning": "fáil: getting, finding", "ctx": "Part of ar fáil, available."}, {"lit": "but", "meaning": "ach: but, only", "ctx": "Here means only by sending an email."}, {"lit": "email", "meaning": "ríomhphost: email", "ctx": "What must be sent."}, {"lit": "to", "meaning": "a: to, verbal particle", "ctx": "Introduces the verbal noun sheoladh."}, {"lit": "send", "meaning": "seol: to send (verbal noun: seoladh, lenited: sheoladh)", "ctx": "Explains how to get the information."}, {"lit": "to", "meaning": "chuig: to", "ctx": "Introduces the email address."}, {"lit": "ceol@rnag.ie", "meaning": "ceol@rnag.ie: email address", "ctx": "The address to send the email to."}, {"lit": "is", "meaning": "is: is", "ctx": "Starts the identification of the final date."}, {"lit": "it", "meaning": "é: it, him", "ctx": "Used in the identifying phrase is é."}, {"lit": "the", "meaning": "an: the", "ctx": "Marks the ordinal date."}, {"lit": "eighth", "meaning": "ochtú: eighth (with t-prefix: t-ochtú)", "ctx": "Part of an t-ochtú lá is fiche, the 28th day."}, {"lit": "day", "meaning": "lá: day", "ctx": "Part of the date phrase."}, {"lit": "and", "meaning": "is: and", "ctx": "In numbers, links eight and twenty."}, {"lit": "20", "meaning": "fiche: twenty", "ctx": "Makes the date twenty-eighth."}, {"lit": "of", "meaning": "de: of", "ctx": "Links the day to the month."}, {"lit": "month", "meaning": "mí: month (lenited after de: mhí)", "ctx": "Part of de mhí Eanáir, of the month of January."}, {"lit": "January", "meaning": "Eanáir: January", "ctx": "Names the month."}, {"lit": "the", "meaning": "an: the", "ctx": "Marks dáta as definite."}, {"lit": "date", "meaning": "dáta: date", "ctx": "The 28th of January is the date."}, {"lit": "last", "meaning": "deireanach: last, final", "ctx": "Describes it as the final date."}, {"lit": "for", "meaning": "le: with, for", "ctx": "Part of le haghaidh, for."}, {"lit": "purpose", "meaning": "aghaidh: face, purpose", "ctx": "Part of le haghaidh, for."}, {"lit": "the", "meaning": "an: the (genitive plural: na)", "ctx": "Marks iontrálacha as definite plural."}, {"lit": "entries", "meaning": "iontráil: entry (plural: iontrálacha, eclipsis: n-iontrálacha)", "ctx": "The deadline is for the entries."}, {"lit": "this", "meaning": "seo: this", "ct